    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Where you live and your address",
     "texto": [
      "To ask where someone lives, say «Waar woon je?». In an affirmative sentence, the verb goes in 2nd position: «Ik woon in Utrecht». To ask for the address: «Wat is je adres?». Notice the nouns with articles: «de straat» (the street), «de stad» (the city), «het dorp» (the village). In Dutch, addresses usually give the street first and then the number: Marktstraat 12."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
